<title>UK: Details of 2.4 pct Feb UK car registrations rise.</title>
<headline>Details of 2.4 pct Feb UK car registrations rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's SMMT Ltd auto trade body issued the following details of car registrations for February on Thursday showing how they rose by 2.4 percent to give a 5.3 percent rise for the first two months of the year so far.</p>
<p>February</p>
<p>Top 10 by marque, market share in pct vs year ago.</p>
<p> Ford	    26,753  (16.42 pct) vs  33,564  (21.11 pct)</p>
<p> GM-Vauxhall   22,054  (13.54 pct) vs  23,979  (15.08 pct)</p>
<p> Rover	   16,655  (10.22 pct) vs  16,634  (10.46 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot	 13,784  (8.64 pct)  vs  11,566   (7.27 pct)</p>
<p> Renault	 13,422  (8.24 pct)  vs  11,516   (7.24 pct)</p>
<p> Volkswagen     8,048  (4.94 pct)  vs   8,097   (5.09 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat	     6,689  (4.11 pct)  vs   7,116   (4.48 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan	   6,075  (3.73 pct)  vs   7,311   (4.60 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota	   5,955  (3.66 pct)  vs   4,358   (2.74 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen	  5,208  (3.20 pct)  vs   5,049   (3.18 pct)</p>
<p>Top 10 marques year to date, market share in pct vs yr ago.</p>
<p> Ford	     67,204 (18.18 pct) vs  75,401  (21.50 pct)</p>
<p> GM-Vauxhall    53,328 (14.16 pct) vs  51,936  (14.81 pct)</p>
<p> Rover	    35,190  (9.52 pct) vs  37,410  (10.66 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot	  28,771  (7.78 pct) vs  26,274   (7.49 pct)</p>
<p> Renault	  28,496  (7.71 pct) vs  23,211   (6.62 pct)</p>
<p> Volkswagen     18,606  (5.03 pct) vs  17,346   (4.95 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen	  16,579  (4.48 pct) vs  14,857   (4.24 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan	   15,005  (4.06 pct) vs  14,788   (4.22 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat	     13,197  (3.57 pct) vs  13,986   (3.99 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota	   12,691  (3.43 pct) vs   9,506   (2.71 pct)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
